About Akuna: &nbsp; 

 Akuna Capital is an innovative trading firm with a strong focus on collaboration,&nbsp;cutting-edge&nbsp;technology, data driven solutions, and automation. We specialize in providing liquidity as an options market&nbsp;maker,&nbsp;meaning we are committed to providing competitive quotes that we are willing to both buy and sell. To do this successfully, we design and implement our own low latency technologies, trading&nbsp;strategies,&nbsp;and mathematical models.&nbsp; &nbsp; 

 Our Founding Partners &nbsp; first conceptualized Akuna in their hometown of Sydney. They opened the firm’s first office in 2011 in the heart of the derivatives industry and the options capital of the world – Chicago. Today, Akuna is proud to&nbsp;operate&nbsp;from&nbsp;additional&nbsp;offices in Sydney, Shanghai, Singapore, and London. &nbsp; 

 What&nbsp;you’ll&nbsp;do as a Platform Engineer Intern at Akuna: &nbsp; &nbsp; 

 We are seeking Platform Engineer Interns to join our innovative and growing technology team for our 10-week&nbsp;Akunacademy&nbsp;internship program.&nbsp;You will&nbsp;work within the Platform Engineering&nbsp;Team, gaining&nbsp;expertise&nbsp;through building highly automated&nbsp;operations while&nbsp;monitoring&nbsp;and managing the operational capabilities of systems at Akuna.&nbsp; Each intern takes full ownership of their project, and at the end of the program, has the opportunity to present their work and accomplishments.&nbsp;In this role, you&nbsp;will:&nbsp; &nbsp; 


 Support and design the ongoing growth, design, and expansion of our Platform offerings to meet the needs of our internal stakeholders with scalable, reliable, and highly available systems &nbsp; 



 Work with our steam aligned and partner platform teams to develop our hybrid cloud platform &nbsp; 



 Produce clean, well-tested, and documented code with a clear design to support&nbsp;production&nbsp;infrastructure and systems&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Challenge the status quo and help push our organization forward, as we grow beyond the limits of our current tech stack&nbsp; &nbsp; 


 &nbsp; Requirements for this role: &nbsp; 


 Pursuing a bachelor’s,&nbsp;master’s, or&nbsp;Ph.D. in a technical field (computer science/engineering, math,&nbsp;physics, or equivalent) &nbsp; 



 Graduating by August 2028 



 Major GPA of 3.5 or above &nbsp; 



 Legal authorization to work in the U.S. is&nbsp;required&nbsp;on the first day of employment including F-1 students using OPT or STEM &nbsp; 


 Previous&nbsp;experience in finance or trading is&nbsp; not &nbsp;required.&nbsp;Many of&nbsp;our&nbsp;engineers&nbsp;joined&nbsp;Akuna with little-to-no&nbsp;prior&nbsp;knowledge&nbsp;of the markets, and we pride ourselves on our ability to onboard those new to the industry. Training and continuous education are provided for all engineers to ensure they can build&nbsp;the requisite technical and non-technical skillset for success. &nbsp; 

 &nbsp; Qualities that make great candidates: &nbsp; &nbsp; 


 Experience with Infrastructure as Code (IaC), Kubernetes,&nbsp;and AWS Cloud&nbsp; &nbsp; 



 Experience with cloud computing, networking, data&nbsp;engineering&nbsp;and security &nbsp; 



 Ability to react quickly and accurately to rapidly changing market conditions, including the ability to quickly and accurately respond and/or solve math and coding problems, is an&nbsp;essential function of the role &nbsp; 


 &nbsp; In addition to the above technical skills, Akuna&nbsp;values diversity of experience and perspective. We believe that&nbsp;engineers with&nbsp;varied backgrounds and interests allow&nbsp;us to&nbsp;approach problems from&nbsp;unique&nbsp;angles&nbsp;and&nbsp;to&nbsp;uncover innovative,&nbsp;optimal&nbsp;solutions.&nbsp;We want everyone to feel empowered to apply; we welcome your application, and we strongly encourage you to take the first steps in joining us&nbsp;in the future! &nbsp; 

 **Resumes must be&nbsp;submitted&nbsp;in PDF format. &nbsp; 

 By&nbsp;applying&nbsp;to this role, you are&nbsp;indicating&nbsp;this is your top preference and acknowledge you will not be considered for other Quant and/or Tech roles at&nbsp;Akuna&nbsp;this recruiting season. This acknowledgement does not limit applications to Trading roles - in addition to this role, you may apply to any Trader roles of interest. &nbsp; 

 We are an AI-friendly company and encourage employees to leverage AI in their daily work. However, AI assistance is not permitted during interviews or assessments . Our interview process is designed to evaluate your individual skills and judgment , and the use of AI tools will result in disqualification from the hiring process. 

 In accordance with&nbsp;the Illinois&nbsp;Equal Pay Act, the&nbsp;minimum&nbsp;annualized base salary starts at $145,000. Exact compensation offered may vary based on many factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and skill set. The minimum base salary&nbsp;herein&nbsp;was&nbsp;determined&nbsp;in good faith by Akuna Capital LLC. &nbsp;
